# The annotations of ATV Simulator's game image, tape block 7 ($6338-$FF77, 40000 bytes, as the loader at $FFDC
# leaves it): the source of src/game/*.asm (../../kit/mkgame.py). Format: ../../../../docs/ann-format.md.
# The recordings (work/stage1/rec, WALKTHROUGH 6): c1 (a 48K from power-on, the original TZX at signal speed, the
# title, the menu, trail 1 to TIME OUT), menu (the menu's pages, two players), kb (the keyboard, redefine), trail1
# (trail 1 ridden to the finish), trails (trails 1-2), warp (trails 3-6 by a POKE of the trail number), fuel (a ride
# at full speed). "Known only from the code" marks what no recording shows.


@equ $4000 Screen 6144 at $6C78,$6DD5,$779C,$779F,$77AA,$77AD,$8CDD,$8CE9,$D8DE,$DA4F,$DA8F,$DFA7,$E511,$E55D,$EB4C,$EE45 ; the screen's pixels
@equ $5800 Attributes 768 at $6A38,$6DDB,$D7FB,$D82F,$DA5B,$DA9B,$ED17 ; the screen's attributes
@equ $5B00 TunePlayerCopy 1451 at $6DEF,$6DFB,$D7DA,$ECE6 ; the tune player's copy (GameEntry's LDIR from $F850), below the image
@equ $60AC Trail6 650 at $D7E5,$ECA8 ; trail 6 as GameEntry copies it from $F230: its record, then its lists
@equ $FFDC StackTop at $D7F2 ; the stack's top: the loader's first byte (GameEntry)
@equ $FFDA StackRestart at $DA0D ; the stack AbortKey restarts on
@isub $8D36 LD SP,BufferP2+$06E0 ; the buffer's end, not the tune player's data
@isub $8D2C LD SP,BufferP1+$06E0 ; the first buffer's end
@isub $F985 LD SP,$F838 ; TunePlay's saved SP: patched, not BufferP2+$011C
@equ $6334 StackBelowImage at $8EB6 ; ItemTooLow's stack: four bytes below the image

@module menu ; The title, the tune's interrupt hook, the menus, the controls, one or two players, the split screen
@about The front end. Title ($6DFB) copies the tune player back from $5B00 to $F850 (the second player's buffer overwrites it in play), shows the credits and the high scores, then MenuLoop ($737C) starts the title tune (TunePlay $F852, tune 0) with the interrupt hook TuneHook pointing at MenuTick ($7340): the menu runs inside the tune player's interrupt until a key stops the tune. A menu is a block of MenuDefs: a count, the box's x and y, its height, then a text and an action per item. The front end draws into the buffer $F03C (22 bytes a line, 80 lines: BufferRows) and copies it to the screen with ShowBuffer or Dissolve.
@about Controls: player 1 has the keyboard (five keys, redefinable) or a Kempston joystick, player 2 the keyboard or a Sinclair joystick (keys 6-0). ReadP1Controls / ReadP2Controls ($D911 / $D942) turn them into five bits each in Controls1 / Controls2: 4 left, 3 right, 2 wheel up, 1 wheel down, 0 jump (fire).

$6338 b MenuGfx 16 ; The front end's graphics bank: 14 pictures, each a sprite and its attributes
> +0 the count (14), +1 the bank's length word ($03C5: it ends at $66FD), +3 zero, then a pair of words a picture from +4: the sprite's offset and the attributes' offset, both from $6338. A sprite is width (bytes), height (lines), advance, shift, then width x height bytes; the attributes are width, height (cells) and a byte a cell. MenuSprite ($863D) and MenuSpriteAttrs ($773D) read it (c1: the title's ATV and logo, the trail intro's number, the panel frames).
@res sprites/menu.bin
$66FD s MenuGfxEnd ; 35 zeros after the bank, never read
$6720 b MenuVars ; The menu's variables
$6720 MenuBoxX ; the current menu box's x (pixels)
$6721 MenuBoxY ; its y (the top line, counted up from the bottom)
$6722 MenuBoxHeight ; its height (lines)
$6723 MenuCount ; its item count
$6724 TuneTimer ; a word counted by MenuTick each frame: the menu falls back to the title (high byte $80) or the high scores ($0400)
$6725 MenuSpare ; written 0 by ClearMenuSpare, never read
$6726 MenuItem ; the highlighted item (0 up)
$6727 w RowAddrs 16 ; The screen address of each of the 192 lines, top first (BuildRowAddrs fills it at the start; zeros in the image)
$68A7 w BufferRows 16 ; The offset of each of the 80 buffer lines (22 bytes a line, from 22: BuildBufferRows fills it)
$6947 b PlayerVars ; Players and scores
$6947 PlayerCount ; 0 one player, 1 two players (MenuPlayerCount toggles it)
$6948 Scores ; the two players' scores, five ASCII digits each; "03000" and "02000" in the image, cleared to "00000" by NewGame
$694D ScoreP2 ; player 2's five digits
$6952 NameColour ; the name entry's colour ($10 player 1, $28 player 2)
$6953 NameRow ; the table row the name goes into
$6954 NameScorePtr ; the row's score
$6956 NameTextPtr ; the row's name
$6958 BigScaleX ; the big print's horizontal scale
$6959 BigScaleY ; its vertical scale (lines a pixel)
$695A BigRepeat ; its repeat
$695B BigClear ; 0 OR the pixels, 1 clear them (the shadow)
$695C CursorPos ; the name entry's cursor (y, x)
$695E BigMask ; the big print's current bit
$695F t HiScoreTitle ; "HI SCORE|" (the table's heading) and "A|" (the trail intro's big digit: TrailIntro writes the trail's character over the A)
@res texts/hiscore.bin
$6968 BigChar ; "A|": a one-character text the trail intro (the trail's digit) and the name entry's letter grid write over
$696A t HiNames ; The high score table's five names, six characters and | each
@res texts/hinames.bin
$6988 t HiScores ; The five scores, five digits and | each: 20000, 15000, 10000, 05000, 03000
@res texts/hiscores.bin
