@module render ; The renderer: the draw modes, the sprites, the buffers, the trail lists, the copy to the screen
@about Everything is drawn into a buffer of 22 bytes x 80 lines (BufferP1 $F03C for the top half, BufferP2 $F71C for the bottom half in a two-player game) and copied to the screen each pass (CopyBuffer, 22 LDIs a line). A sprite is a header (width in bytes, height in lines, advance, shift) and its bytes, line by line from the top; SpriteHeader ($865F) reads it into SpriteWidth.. and DrawSprite calls the current draw mode through ModeVector: the word table DrawModes for the front end, ListModes for the trail. There are no shifted copies: when SpriteX AND 7 differs from the shift a sprite's +3 byte keeps, SpriteHeader has ShiftLeftBy / ShiftRightBy (RotateSpriteLeft / RotateSpriteRight, a bit at a time over the whole sprite) move its bytes in place, and the bank stays so. In c1's heaviest pass (tools/pass_time.py: c1 frame 15356, 438 645 T, 89.7 % of the 7 frames) the two rotate routines take 31 % of the CPU, re-shifting the START sign's sprites ($7B 9 x 31, $A5 5 x 45) as they scroll off the left edge, with a landing's Tone.
$69F7 w DrawModes 1 ; The front end's draw modes: a routine each, picked by ModeVector ($82F8 points at the word in use)
> +0 ModeNone (RET: measure only), +2 ModeCopyScreen, +4 ModeOrScreen (no caller), +6 ModeXorScreen, +8 ModeCopyBuffer, +10 ModeXorBuffer, +12 ModeAttrsNone (RET), +14 ModeAttrsCopy (no caller), +16 BigPrint.

@module menu
$6A09 c LoadIntro ; The intro before the first menu: clear, a checkered band, the ATV and the boxes of the loading picture
> Clears the screen (ClearScreen), draws a checkered band (Checker) and the sprite list LoadIntroSprites with the menu bank, then the attribute boxes LoadIntroBoxes. Called through JpLoadIntro by NewGame.
> Witness: L1 7 (c1, empty, fuel, kb, trail1, trails, warp).
$6A38 c TrailIntro ; The trail's intro: "TRAIL NO." and the trail's number in big print, the name, the panels
> Clears the screen's attributes and pixels, prints TrailNoText twice (shadow and face) at scale 2 x 5, the trail's number (Trail + "b", a big digit) at scale 2 x 4, dissolves the buffer onto the screen, waits 50 frames, copies the trail's name (CopyTrailName) and prints it and the intro picture (TrailIntroBoxes), waits 150 frames, then draws one or two players' panels (PanelP1, PanelP2), each coloured by TrailAttrs. Called through JpTrailIntro before each trail (c1 frame 15 800).
> Witness: L1 16 (c1, empty, fuel, kb, trail1, trails, warp).
$6B3B c FillColumn ; Write E into B lines down from HL (screen)
> Witness: L1 3136 (c1, empty, fuel, kb, trail1, trails, warp).
$6B42 c PanelP2 ; The second player's half: its frame, its HUD, the FUEL and SPEED bars
> The bottom half's sprite list PanelP2Sprites, the side lines (E = $0F / $F0 down 88 lines), the record copy (CopyRecordP2), the HUD at y 6, ShowBars, ShowMaxTime and the attribute boxes PanelP2Boxes. Only in a two-player game (menu: 2 runs).
> Witness: L1 2 (kb).
$6B8C c PanelP1 ; The first player's half: its frame, its HUD, the bars
> As PanelP2 for the top half (y $BE).
> Witness: L1 16 (c1, empty, fuel, kb, trail1, trails, warp).
