@module scores ; The high score table and the name entry; the clock, the finish, the score, the lap, EXTENDED PLAY, TIME OUT
@about The score is five ASCII digits a player (Scores $6948 / $694D): one point up for each $1000 of distance forwards ($D789 bit 12 changing, ScoreUpP1 / ScoreUpP2), one down backwards, and at the trail's end the time bonus counted in by TrailEnd with the EXTENDED PLAY sound. The clock (Clock $D6C9-$D6CB, three ASCII digits) counts up once a second of passes (ClockTick); a trail ends at the finish (both riding players past FinishDistance) or at TIME OUT when the clock reaches the trail's maximum (MaxTimes: 60, 60, 60, 40, 50, 50). After the game CheckHiScore compares each score with the table HiScores and runs the name entry for a place.
$7A3E c CheckHiScore ; After a game: each player's score into the table when it beats a row, with the name entry
> Player 1 against the five rows (HiCompare); in a two-player game player 2 too. A place: NameEntry with the player's reader (ReadP1 $7BBE or ReadP2 $7BC2) patched into ReadControlJump. Called through JpCheckHiScore by GameEntry's outer loop after each game (c1: 4 runs, 2 places).
> Witness: L1 4 (c1, kb, trail1, warp).
$7A7E c NameEntry ; Insert the score at its row (moving the rows below down), then enter the name on a letter grid
> A the row (HiCompare). The scores and names below move down by LDDR, the score goes in, the name is blanked; the screen shows the table, the grid of letters A-Z, space and the end mark (4 rows of 7), a cursor moved by the player's controls (left/right/up/down), fire takes the letter under it into the name; the end mark returns.
> Witness: L1 5 (c1, kb, trail1, warp).
