@module trails ; The six trails: the records, the object lists, the animated objects
@about A trail is a record of three words (TrailRecords for trails 1-4, Trail5 $EE84, Trail6 $60AC copied from $F230 by GameEntry): list A (the ground and the obstacles the ATV rides over and hits), list B (the scenery behind: drawn after the ATV's ground test, so it never stops it), and the length; FinishDistance = the length - $48. A list is items of six bytes in order of distance: +0 the distance word, +2 y (0: the sprite's height, filled by InitListWidths), +3 the advance (filled by InitListWidths), +4 the sprite number and +5 the flags (bit 0 mirrored, bits 1-3 the draw mode: 1 deferred to DeferredA, 2 to DeferredB); flags bits 4-7 set make +4/+5 the address of an animation record instead. $FF at +1 ends a list. List A scrolls with the distance (Distance $D789-$D78B, a step of speed x 128 a pass), list B at an eighth of it ($D78E-$D790, speed x 16).
$7C9C b TrailRecords 6 ; Trails 1-4: list A, list B, length
> Read by SelectTrail ($EC9C) as TrailRecords + 6 x Trail (c1: trail 1; trails: trails 1-2; warp: 3-4).
@res trails/trails14.bin
$7CB4 b Trail1ListA 6 ; Trail 1's list A (the ground and obstacles)
@res trails/trails14.bin
$7D34 b Trail2ListA 6 ; Trail 2's list A
@res trails/trails14.bin
$7E20 b Trail3ListA 6 ; Trail 3's list A
@res trails/trails14.bin
$7F00 b Trail4ListA 6 ; Trail 4's list A
@res trails/trails14.bin
$7F80 b Trail1ListB 6 ; Trail 1's list B (the scenery)
@res trails/trails14.bin
$7FB2 b Trail2ListB 6 ; Trail 2's list B
@res trails/trails14.bin
