> +0 the count (203), +1 the bank's length word ($471E: it ends at $D67A), +3 zero, from +4 a word a sprite: its header's offset from $8F5C. Headers as SpriteHeader reads them; the shift byte (+3) is 0 in the image and changes in play. Twelve gaps of two or four bytes between sprites and the 54 bytes $D67A-$D6AF after the last are bytes no offset reaches (the end of a sprite's bytes in an older bank).
> ZXDB POKE 49433,81 ("infinite fuel") writes $51 over byte 46 of sprite 126 ($C119, its line 7): a pixel byte, no effect on the fuel (recording pokes).
