@module loop ; The entry's jumps, the game's variables, the main loop with its 7-frame wait, the interrupt
@about GameEntry ($D7D6) copies the tune player and trail 6 out of the buffers' way, sets up IM 2 (I = $FE, a table of $80 bytes, the vector $8080 = JP Interrupt) and runs the outer loop: Title, NewGame, CheckHiScore. NewGame clears the scores and runs the trails: Pass ($D851) is one pass of the game for both players, then it waits until the interrupt has counted FrameCount up to 7, so a pass is always 7 frames (7.14 passes a second) when its work fits. Interrupt ($D9D2) counts the frames in play and plays the engines' tones; in the front end (FrameCount $FF) it reads the controls.
$D6B0 c EntryJumps ; JP GameEntry; JP Restart
> The loader enters at $D6B0 (c1 frame 14 100); ItemTooLow jumps to Restart at $D6B3.
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$D6B3 RestartJump
$D6B6 b LoopVars ; The game's variables
$D6B6 TrailListA ; the trail's list A (SelectTrail)
$D6B8 TrailListB ; the trail's list B
$D6BA SavedSp0 ; SP at the entry
$D6BC FrameCount ; frames counted by Interrupt since the pass began; $FF in the front end (the interrupt reads the controls instead)
$D6BE Riding ; the players still in: bit 0 player 1, bit 1 player 2
$D6BF Trail ; the trail, 0-5
$D6C0 FinishDistance ; the trail's length - $48: a player whose distance reaches it has finished
$D6C2 HudY ; the half's HUD line ($BE top, 6 bottom)
$D6C3 PassControls ; the current player's controls this pass
$D6C4 GroundY ; the ground under the ATV's wheels (GroundUnder): the higher of $D6C5 (rear) and $D6C6 (front); $D6C7 under the nose, $D6C8 the nose's line
$D6C9 Clock ; the clock: three ASCII digits; the last one counts passes (ClockTick), not seconds
$D6CA ClockTens
$D6CB ClockUnits
$D6CC MaxTime ; the trail's maximum: the clock's first two digits at TIME OUT ("60" = 600 passes)
$D6CF MaxTimes ; each trail's maximum: "60", "60", "60", "40", "50", "50"; "30" in the second round (ShowMaxTime)
$D6DB c GameTable ; The game's jump table; the first entry JP TrailEnd
> The entries at $D6DE, $D6ED, $D6F0, $D6F3, $D6FC, $D702, $D705 and $D708 are called by no one (known only from the code; $D702 is JP $0000).
> Known only from the code: no recording runs it.
