@module vehicle ; The ATV and its rider: the records, the controls, speed, steering, wheelies, jumps, the ground, crashes, tumbling, the rider on foot, mounting, fuel
@about Each player has a record of 50 bytes (RecordP1 $D70E, RecordP2 $D740); the pass copies it to Record ($D772) and back. The ATV moves along the trail by Distance (speed x 128 a pass), never sideways: Left and Right are the throttle in the facing direction (Accelerate, up to speed level 21) and the brake against it (SlowDown by 2); at a standstill the brake turns the ATV round (the riderless frame $5C while it turns). Up lifts the nose (WheelieUp, 10 passes of WheelieTimer), Down drops it; Jump sets an upward speed from $FD less the slope. GroundUnder scans the buffer's pixels under the wheels: the ground is whatever list A drew there. A drop of 7 or more lines on landing or a step of $15 crashes (Crash): under speed 10 the ATV stops, 10-14 it stops and throws the rider, 15 and up it tumbles (Tumble, 24 passes) and throws the rider. The thrown rider lands lying ($77); Jump stands him up; on foot Left / Right walk him (3 pixels a pass) and Jump jumps; landing on the ATV from behind while facing its way remounts (MountCheck). Fuel ($2000 at each trail) drops by speed x 2 a moving pass; the FUEL bar loses 4 pixels each $400; under $400 the ATV is out of fuel (OutOfFuel: never reached in the recordings).
$D70E b RecordP1 ; Player 1's record (50 bytes, Record's fields), copied in and out each pass
$D740 b RecordP2 ; Player 2's record
$D772 b Record ; The current player's record
$D772 RiderJump ; the rider's jump on foot: 0 on the ground, 1-7 its phase (RiderJumpTable)
$D773 VSpeed ; the ATV's vertical speed: $FD-$F8 rising (negative), 1-5 falling (FallSteps)
$D774 Mounted ; 1 the rider is on the ATV, 0 on foot
$D775 AtvFrame ; the ATV's sprite: $38-$45 nose up by steps of 2, $46-$4E nose down, $5C riderless, $7D-$87 tumbling
$D776 Facing ; 0 right, 1 left
$D777 AtvX ; the ATV's x on screen
$D778 AtvHeight ; its height above the bottom line
$D779 PrevHeight ; the height a pass ago ($D77A two passes ago)
$D77B Speed ; the speed level, 0-21
$D77C Fuel ; the fuel word ($2000 full; empty under $400)
$D77E SpeedBarLen ; the SPEED bar's drawn length
$D77F FuelBar ; the FUEL bar's end x ($90 + the length)
$D780 JumpLatch ; 1 while jump is held (one jump a press)
$D781 TurnLeft ; 1 while the ATV turns round to the left
$D782 TurnRight ; 1 while it turns to the right
$D783 RiderFrame ; the rider's sprite: 0-8 walking, $18 jumping, $59 riding, $5E-$64 thrown, $77 lying
$D784 RiderFacing ; 0 right, 1 left
$D785 RiderX ; the rider's x
$D786 RiderHeight ; the rider's height
$D787 RiderSavedX ; the rider's x a pass ago (put back when he walks into a step)
$D788 RiderSavedHeight
$D789 Distance ; the distance along the trail, 24 bits ($D789 the fraction)
$D78A TrackPos ; the distance's whole part: list A's scroll; FinishCheck compares it with FinishDistance
$D78C DistanceIndex ; list A's index (WalkList)
$D78E Scenery ; list B's scroll, 24 bits
$D78F SceneryPos ; its whole part
$D791 ScenIndex ; list B's index
$D795 WheelieTimer ; passes the nose stays up after Up or a jump
$D797 TumbleCount ; passes of tumbling (0 none)
$D798 FallPhase ; the rider's fall when thrown at a step (FallRider: no recording)
$D799 ThrowSpeed ; the thrown rider's flight: $F8 - speed / 8 up, then down
$D79A EngineNote ; bit 7 the engine's tone on, bits 0-4 the passes to the next change (EngineTimer)
$D79B Bonus ; the time bonus, counted into the score at the trail's end
$D79D LapTime ; the clock at the finish (three digits)
$D7A0 GroundBelowRider ; the ground under the rider
$D7A4 b BeeperByte ; The last byte sent to port $FE (bit 4 the speaker), toggled by Click
$D7A5 Finished ; the players past the finish: bit 0 player 1, bit 1 player 2
$D7A6 SecondRound ; 1 after trail 6: the trails again with 30 as every maximum
$D7A7 RecordTemplate ; a new record (InitRecords): frame $38, x $48, fuel $2000, the bars, the engine 1, lap "000"; its last three bytes are GameEntry's first instruction

@module entry ; The entry: the copies out of the buffers' way, the initialisation, IM 2
@about The 40000-byte block fills $6338-$FF77, so the game keeps work areas inside its own image: BufferP1 ($F03C-$F71B) lies over trail 6 as loaded ($F230), BufferP2 ($F71C-$FDFB) over the tune player ($F850-$FDFA). GameEntry first copies the tune player to $5B00-$60AB (Title and TrailEnd copy it back before a tune) and trail 6 to $60AC-$6335, just under the image, then the stack goes to $FFDC (the loader's place).
$D7D6 c GameEntry ; Copy the tune player and trail 6 out, initialise, set IM 2, then the outer loop: Title, NewGame, CheckHiScore
> Entered from the loader's JP $D6B0 (c1 frame 14 100). LDIR $F850-$FDFA to $5B00 ($5AB bytes), $F230-$F4B9 to $60AC ($28A bytes); DI, SP = $FFDC, Init, SetupIm2.
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$D7ED Restart ; the restart after ItemTooLow: SP, Init, SetupIm2, the outer loop
$D7FB OuterLoop ; AttrBase = $5800, Title, NewGame, CheckHiScore, again

@module loop
$D80D c NewGame ; A game: trail 1, scores "00000", the riding mask from Players; each trail: select, intro, panels, then Pass until the finish or TIME OUT
> Trail = 0, SecondRound = 0, Riding = 1 or 3 (PlayerCount); LoadIntro; then for each trail SelectTrail, FrameCount = $FF, InitListWidths, InitRecords, TrailIntro, ShowHud, ClearKeys, EI, and the passes. TrailEnd jumps back to NextTrail ($D82F).
$D82F NextTrail
$D851 Pass ; One pass: the controls, the clock, both players' updates, then wait for 7 frames; the finish and TIME OUT
> FrameCount = 0, ReadP1Controls, ReadP2Controls, ClearKeys, ClockTick, Players; then the wait loop on FrameCount (c1: 30 269 229 runs of $D86B over 5081 passes). Both players' Finished bits set (as Riding) end the trail (TrailEnd); the clock's first digit equal to MaxTime's: TIME OUT for both (TimeOut), then TrailEnd when someone finished, else 250 frames and the game ends.
> Witness: L1 7 (c1, empty, fuel, kb, trail1, trails, warp).
$D86B WaitFrames
$D88A c RecordFieldP1 ; A = RecordP1's field +9 (speed), Z when 0
> Witness: L1 5351 (c1, empty, fuel, kb, trail1, trails, warp).
$D890 c RecordFieldP2 ; A = RecordP2's field +9
> Witness: L1 3592 (c1, empty, fuel, kb, trail1, trails, warp).
$D8C3 c Init ; Controls off (player 2 on the keyboard... SinclairOn = 1), DetectKempston, the row tables, the text widths, FrameCount = $FF
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$D8ED c SetupIm2 ; IM 2: I = $FE, the table $FE00-$FF00 all $80, JP Interrupt at $8080
> Witness: L1 20 (c1, empty, fuel, kb, menu, trail1, trails, warp).
$D911 c ReadP1Controls ; Controls1 = player 1's five tests as bits (4 left, 3 right, 2 up, 1 down, 0 jump)
> Witness: L1 24779 (c1, empty, fuel, kb, menu, trail1, trails, warp).
$D942 c ReadP2Controls ; Controls2 from player 2's tests
> Witness: L1 24779 (c1, empty, fuel, kb, menu, trail1, trails, warp).
$D974 c RecordField ; A = (IX + DE), Z when 0
